# Explore the Five-Vertex Path Inequality

A symmetric weighted network compresses its four-edge path count into two matrix–vector products. Begin with the sharp boundary: every constant kernel lies exactly on it.

{{interactive_demo:0}}

## From five nested sums to two propagation steps

The first algorithm computes the degree vector $d=A\mathbf 1$, propagates it once more to $u=Ad$, and returns $P=\|u\|_2^2$. This costs $O(n^2)$ for dense matrices rather than enumerating $n^5$ maps.

